ana (Presales): Quick sync: AcmeRetail wants a compact POC next week. Goals: websocket streaming + function calls for inventory checks -> structured JSON output. Also need EU data residency, BYOK, and rough committed pricing for 10k qps baseline.
conrad (Eng): Ok. Main dev work: Rust SDK currently returns raw frames; we should emit events: token, function_call, function_result. Node/Python already do that.
leo (Solutions): For demo we can show websocket streaming where tokens come as they generate and a final function_result event with a JSON payload. Should cover both incremental UI updates and full JSON ingestion.
nana (Presales): (typo correction) ana: They clarified 10k qps is peak expected, average closer to 1k-2k. Also 70% of calls are small completions (<50 tokens). That helps.
conrad (Eng): Good—that changes capacity planning. For POC recommend throttling to 500qps sustained to validate infra. We'll provide a sample Node + Rust example that does: open ws -> send prompt + function list -> stream tokens -> on function_call event call dummy inventory API -> return function_result.
conrad (Eng): Node snippet:
```js
const ws = client.ws({model:'r-infer-1'});
ws.send({input: prompt, functions:[{name:'lookup_item',parameters:{type:'object'}}]});
ws.on('token', t => ui.append(t));
ws.on('function_call', fc => { // call internal api
  const res = lookup(fc.arguments);
  ws.send({function_result: {name: fc.name, result: res}});
});
```
conrad (Eng): Rust sketch (pseudo):
```rs
let mut socket = Client::connect(...);
socket.send(request);
while let Some(evt) = socket.next().await {
  match evt { Token(t) => ..., FunctionCall(fc) => { let res = call_internal(fc.args); socket.send(FunctionResult{...}).await }, FunctionResult(fr) => ... }
}
```
leo (Solutions): I'll prep a tiny shim crate that turns function_result into serde_json::Value so customers can parse regardless of strict schema. Ship with README and quickstart.
tina (Security): Checklist: SOC2 link (attached), BYOK options: - Dedicated with KMS passthrough (customer key via cloud KMS) - Private with customer HSM - No customer data persisted by default; logs/metrics stored for 30d. For POC we can configure minimal retention and EU where needed. Need PO if they want dedicated infra access.
nana (Presales): (again) ana: Legal: MSA signed; no NDA required for sample code. If they want dedicated test cluster, require PO + security review.
leo (Solutions): Pricing note: with revised averages (70% <50 tokens) the token load is much smaller. Back-of-envelope: assume avg tokens per request = 60 -> 10k qps => 600k tokens/sec => 36M tokens/min. Still large. For POC present two options: 1) Reduced POC traffic (500qps) for validation 2) Full capacity proposal: Dedicated cluster estimate = 8x A100 equiv reserved + 12-month commit for best price. For POC offer 40% dev discount for 3 months. Final numbers once we model real token distribution.
conrad (Eng): Ops note: ensure client side validates both object typed function results and falls back to string parsing. Add this to runbook acceptance. Also include telemetry hooks: per-request latency, tokens-in/out, function call success rate.
nana (Presales): Action list: 1) I'll confirm avg tokens by call type and % streaming vs simple completion with Acme 2) Leo to open draft repo + Rust shim + README 3) Tina to send security checklist + SOC2 link and retention options 4) Conrad to push Node + Rust minimal examples to GH and confirm event names.
conrad (Eng): Pushed initial repo + sample runtime to staging. CI: build 4521 started.
